wishnode.net — Forms Intake Router page content phext (phexts/forms-router.phext). Source of truth for the Forms Intake Router page. Task 34.6.6/7.7.10/7.6.10. See docs/COORDINATE-MAP.md.Forms Intake Router — Exocortexia | Phext, Inc.Forms Intake RouterForms intake with a fixed set of steps — and no personal information by designSUMMARY (plain English — rendered first)The Forms Intake Router takes in forms and sends each one to the office that owns it. The person who sent the form gets a tracking code and can check its state at any time. The form asks for no name and no contact details, so there is no personal data to protect or to lose.What it doesOffices get forms each day. The demo is built for public-records requests. Each form must be sorted, sent to the right office, worked, and closed. The person who sent it should be able to see where it stands.This tool makes each step clear and on the record. Nothing drifts. Nothing is closed in secret.No personal information, by designThe form asks for four things: the agency, the subject, a short description, and a date range. There is no field for a name, an email, or a phone number. Routing a form needs none of those, so the form never asks.The form page shows a clear notice: SAMPLE DATA ONLY — DO NOT ENTER PERSONAL INFORMATION.When a form is sent, the sender gets a tracking code. The code is made from the form and its contents by a standard math method (SHA-256). The sender checks the state of the form with the code alone. No account is needed. No email is needed.Fixed steps, in a fixed orderEach form moves through four states, in this order: received, then routed, then in review, then closed. Those three moves are the just legal moves. There are 16 ways two states could pair up. The rest are not allowed.Our tests try all 16 pairs. A move that skips a step, such as routed straight to closed, is refused. When a move is refused, nothing is written. No state changes. No log entry is made.Why this matters: in most intake systems, the steps are not written down. States drift. Forms end up in states no one planned. Writing the steps down, and testing the banned moves too, turns a label into a promise.Forms can be saved out as a standard spreadsheet file (CSV), with the code, the form kind, the state, the agency, and the subject.What the law saysThe demo form is a public-records request. Nebraska law (§ 84-712) gives each person the right to see public records. Each request must reach the right office and be answered under that law. Intake is part of that legal duty, not just office work.Check the current law for reply due dates and fees before you cite them. This page is a guide, not legal advice.Small state web forms have most often been built through the state's web portal team. A tool of this size fits that pattern: one form family, one set of steps, hosted in a simple way.Full sheet: see the Forms Router part of the statutes phext on this site. The page link reads “How the Forms Router matches Nebraska law.”Good to knowAll forms in the demo are made up.The form itself is set by a data spec, not fixed in code. To change the form, staff change the spec.The suite is checked by 69 automated tests. Eleven of them check this program, and they try all 16 state pairs.Ask about a pilotAsk about a pilot for your office. Use the form on this site — the link says “Ask about a pilot.” Tell us which program you are interested in and what your office needs. When you send the form, you get a tracking code. Keep it. You can use it on this site to check the state of your request at any time. We read every request, and a person from Phext, Inc. replies. We will talk through what a small pilot would look like for your office. There is no cost to ask, and asking does not sign you up for anything.Links on this page (descriptive labels)Read the Forms Intake Router source code (for programmers) — Source tree in the Exocortexia repositoryHow the Forms Router matches Nebraska law — State-machine sheet, also held in phexts/statutes.phextFOR TECHNICAL STAFF — not main copy. Component: apps/forms-router · Default port: 8805 · Tests: 11 in this app, 69 workspace-wide · Tracking code: first 10 hex chars of sha256(form + sequence + values) · Illegal transition: HTTP 400, nothing written · Export: RFC 4180 CSV (code, form, state, agency, subject) · Sign-in: edit.phext.io SSO when configured; open demo mode otherwise · Source: github.com/wbic16/Exocortexia/tree/exo/apps/forms-router · Sheet source: docs/forms-router-statute.md.Original page text before the plain-English rewrite (provenance):
